00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:55.180
LG AI research released XAON 4.5. It's first open-weight vision language model. They built it by adding

00:01:55.180 --> 00:02:01.460
a dedicated visual encoder to the XAON 4.0 tech backbone. The model was trained with heavy emphasis on

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:06.920
curated document centric corpora. That focus delivers strong gains in document understanding and

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:13.340
Korean contextual reasoning while extending context to 256,000 tokens. It competes well on general

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:19.500
benchmarks and outperforms same-scale models on document tasks. Enterprises working with PDFs,

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:25.160
forms, or Korean language content should evaluate it immediately. An independent researcher using a

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:32.240
custom tensor distribution diagnostic found that Gemma 4.26b exhibits severe issues. The model shows

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:38.060
KL divergence drift in 21 of 29 affected tensors, almost all belonging to attention layers.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:44.300
In contrast, when 3.5.35 billion showed healthy attention distributions with only a single broken

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:49.900
layer, the analysis suggests Gemma 4 shipped with a systemic architectural or training flaw that

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:54.660
standard benchmarks missed. Anyone running Gemma 4 in production should test against this

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:59.920
diagnostic before trusting outputs on long or complex sequences. A new survey formalizes medical

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.920
reasoning as iterative abduction, deduction, and induction cycles. The authors evaluate both

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:09.760
training-based and training-free methods under unified conditions. They introduce MRBench built

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:14.640
from real hospital data. It reveals a large gap between exam style performance and genuine

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:20.060
clinical decision accuracy. The work gives practitioners a clear map of current limitations in a

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:26.240
harder benchmark for future medical-large language models. Zero ID is a new open source identity and

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:31.940
authentication platform built specifically for autonomous AI agents operating across untrusted

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:38.280
environments. It addresses core needs around verifiable identity, authorization, and auditability

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:44.960
that generic auth systems ignore when the principle is software rather than a human. Developers building

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:51.060
multi-agent systems or agents that cross organizational boundaries can integrate it today. Doing so

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:56.820
should reduce spoofing and permission creep risks right from the start. Many Max open sourced

00:03:56.820 --> 00:04:03.440
MMX CLI, a node.js command line tool. It exposes their full omnimodal stack including image, video,

