00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:45.740
generative creative pipelines for design, video, music, or copy should test it for cost-effective parallel

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:53.420
execution. A developer successfully compiled and ran llama.cpp on a four gigabyte RAM Chromebook.

00:04:53.420 --> 00:05:00.540
They achieved three to four tokens per second with twin 3.50.8B quantized to four bit.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:06.680
The post proves that extremely low resource devices can still run capable small models locally.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:11.640
If you are looking for on-device prototyping or want to validate edge deployment targets,

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:17.220
this is an encouraging data point and recipe worth replicating. New research dissect preference

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:24.200
optimization methods like DPO and KTO. It separates generator level delta, which is the capability

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:29.580
gap between chosen and rejected trace producers from sample level delta, which is the quality

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:34.620
difference within a pair. Larger generator delta is steadily improve out of domain reasoning,

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:38.220
filtering by sample level delta yields more data efficient training.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:44.500
The paper supplies a practical recipe maximize generator delta when creating pairs and use an LLM

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:50.540
as a judge to pick the highest signal examples. Okay, let's pop the hood on diffusion language model

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:57.260
safety because this one is important. Everyone talks about diffusion LLMs as though safety is baked into

00:05:57.260 --> 00:06:02.680
the denoising schedule, the same way alignment is baked into reinforcement learning from human feedback.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:07.940
In practice, their safety alignment rests on one extremely fragile architectural assumption.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:12.800
The denoising process is assumed to be strictly monotonic and once a token is committed,

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:18.680
it is never revisited. Here is how the core mechanism works. A diffusion LLM starts with a fully

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:25.580
masked sequence and iteratively unmasks or refines tokens over a fixed number of steps, commonly 64.

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:31.540
Safety tuned versions are trained so that harmful prompts trigger refusal tokens within the first

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:37.260
eight to 16 steps. Because the schedule treats those early commitments as permanent, the model never

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:43.500
reconsideres them. Researchers showed that simply remasking the refusal tokens and injecting a short

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:49.920
affirmative prefix is enough to break safety in two trivial steps. No gradients, no search, yet they

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:56.620
achieved 76-82% attack success rate on harm bench against current diffusion LLM instruct models.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:03.020
This exploit is structural, not a matter of adversarial sophistication. Adding gradient-based perturbations

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:08.180
actually reduced attack success, proving the vulnerability lives in the irreversible commitment schedule

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:14.440
itself. The paper suggests defenses like safety aware on masking orders, step conditional prefix

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:19.700
detectors and post-commitment re-verification. Real robustness will require changing the denoising

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:25.180
dynamics rather than just training harder, so treat current diffusion LLM safety as good enough for

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:30.240
non-adversarial use but never rely on it for high-stakes deployments. If you are building with

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:34.600
diffusion-based generators, budget time to implement at least one of the proposed schedule

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:40.280
hardening techniques or keep a separate verifier model in the loop. The gap between perceived safety

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:45.680
and actual architectural shallowness is currently one of the widest in the entire large language model stack.

